### MCP

Run the Model Context Protocol server:

```bash
{{github_repo_name}}{% if primary_component != 'mcp' %}-mcp{% endif %}
```
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_worker %}

### Worker

Run the message queue worker:

```bash
{{github_repo_name}}{% if primary_component != 'worker' %}-worker{% endif %}
```

The worker connects to {{worker_broker}} and processes messages from the configured queues.

The worker is tested at two levels. Fast unit tests use FastStream's in-memory
`Test{{ 'Rabbit' if worker_broker == 'rabbitmq' else worker_broker|capitalize }}Broker` and run as part of the default suite on
every platform — they need no running {{worker_broker}}. A separate integration
test (marked `integration`) spins up a real {{worker_broker}} via
[testcontainers](https://testcontainers.com/) and is excluded from the default
run; execute it explicitly (Docker required):

```bash
uv run --locked tox run -e integration
```
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_profiling %}

### Profiling

Profile your application for performance optimization:

```bash
# Setup profiling environment
tox run -e profile

# Profile with scalene (CPU/memory)
python profile.py scalene

# Profile with cProfile (built-in)
python profile.py cprofile

# Profile with py-spy (sampling, low overhead)
py-spy top -- python profile.py run
```

View cProfile results with:

```bash
snakeviz profile.prof
```
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_c_extensions %}

### C Extensions

This package includes high-performance C extensions compiled with Cython.

```python
from {{github_repo_name}} import ExampleExtension, fibonacci_cython

# Use the Cython extension class
ext = ExampleExtension(42)
print(ext.get_value())  # 42

# Use the Cython function
result = fibonacci_cython(10)
print(result)  # 55
```

If Cython compilation fails during installation, the package will fall back to pure Python implementations.
{%- endif %}
{% endif %}
